findings.detail:
The diff also changes local.py:
- it drops the foot_*_land_* offsets from the movable set, citing a 'founder decision 2026-11-16' that has no ADR in project/decisions;
- it adds the BUDGET kind;
- it changes checkpoint keys to include solvers.tag, which invalidates existing checkpoints;
- it adds LocalConfig validation.
In test_local_search, the world fixture is now chosen by scanning rng seeds 3 to 59 for one that gives an 8 mm Manhattan seed, and a tie-order test now runs with reach=False. The movable-set change agrees with the objective's scope_in ('columns, slots, die rows, landing lines'), and all 62 local/search tests pass, so this is a matter of provenance and scope.
